WEBVTT

1
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Subtitles by explosiveskull
Resync by GoldenBeard

2
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Budapest.

3
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.000
The next stop's Budapest.

4
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Budapest is the next stop.

5
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Budapest.

6
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Tickets, ladies.

7
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Oop, here you go.

8
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.000
- Here's mine.
- And mine.

9
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.000
- Mine, too!
- Here you go!

10
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Thank you, young man.

11
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Man, I hate wearing disguises.

12
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.000
These heels are killing me.

13
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Okay, take it down a notch.

14
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.000
We don't want to alarm
the humans.

15
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.000
Psst. Drac.

16
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.000
I'm about to und freak out!

17
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.000
You're a nice kitty.

18
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.000
I'm und kitty-cat.

19
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Meow. Meow!

20
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.000
Oh, no,
not this clown again.

21
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Good evening, travelers.

22
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.000
I am Professor
Abraham Van Helsing.

23
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Yes. One of the Van Helsings.

24
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.000
For centuries, my family
has protected humanity

25
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.000
from the evils of monsters.

26
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.000
So you can believe me
when I tell you,

27
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.000
there are monsters
hiding amongst you!

28
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.000
But fear not,

29
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.000
for I am a professional,
and I know how to flush out

30
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.000
these beasts
and bring them into the light!

31
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.000
Fire bad!

32
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.000
Whoa!

33
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.000
Sorry, guys.

34
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.000
Finally! First I kill Dracula,

35
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.000
and then
the rest of the monsters!

36
00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.000
Why do you keep doing this?

37
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.000
Your dad, your grandfather,
your great-great-granny...

38
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.000
I defeated them all.

39
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.000
When will you Van Helsings ever
learn to let go of the hate?

40
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:15.000
Never! Because you,
monster, are a...

41
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.000
Eh, squeak, squeak.

42
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.000
What? A mouse?

43
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.000
Ahhh!

44
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.000
You can't run from me,
Prince of Darkness!

45
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.000
I will hunt you
for all eternity!

46
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:33.000
I swear I will never rest until
I destroy you...

47
00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.000
And...

48
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.000
Every...

49
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.000
Other...

50
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.000
Monster... Ow!

51
00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.000
If it's the last thing...

52
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.000
I...

53
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.000
Ever...

54
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.000
Do!

55
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.000
Boy, that guy is annoying.

56
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.000
Maybe one day
there will be a place

57
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.000
where monsters can go
to get away from it all,

58
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.000
take a vacation.

59
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.000
Who knows,
maybe even get married.

60
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.000
Wouldn't that be something?

61
00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.000
Hmm?

62
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.000
It's okay.

63
00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.000
Oh, when is
this thing starting?

64
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.000
Aw, you made them cry,
Wayne.

65
00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.000
All except this little one.
Coochie-coochie...

66
00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:57.000
That's Sunny.
She doesn't cry.

67
00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.000
She bites.

68
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:02.000
This is a very special moment, Carl.

69
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:08.000
Any second, your beautiful bride is
going to walk right down the aisle.

70
00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.000
Oh, no, Drac,
she's not coming.

71
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.000
Oh, don't worry.

72
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:17.000
Mavis is with her. I'm sure
everything is under control.

73
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:20.000
Mavey, is everything
under control?

74
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:24.000
Um, yep, just a slight case
of pre-wedding jitters.

75
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.000
Ahhh!

76
00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.000
Yep, everything is
fine here.

77
00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.000
Please try to relax, Lucy.

78
00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.000
I've taken care
of everything.

79
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.000
The wedding
is going to be perfect.

80
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.000
It's not that.

81
00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:49.000
Just, how do I know
I'm doing the right thing?

82
00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.000
I know just how you feel.

83
00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.000
The day I married Johnny was
the best day of my life,

84
00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.000
but I was so nervous.

85
00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Not as nervous
as I was.

86
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.000
And you should have seen my dad.
He was a mess.

87
00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.000
I wouldn't get out
of my coffin that night.

88
00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.000
But he knew
it was meant to be.

89
00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.000
It doesn't matter
where you come from

90
00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.000
or how different
you are.

91
00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:14.000
A Zing only happens
once in your life,

92
00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.000
and you have to
cherish it.

93
00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.000
Aw.

94
00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:22.000
You're right! Thank you!

95
00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.000
Okay.
All right. Okay.

96
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.000
Oh. Uh... Okay.

97
00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.000
I do.

98
00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.000
I do.

99
00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.000
Do you hear that?

100
00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.000
Yes. I thought we
locked him in his room.

101
00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.000
We did!

102
00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.000
Whoa! Whoa!

103
00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.000
Hi, Mom. Hi, Papa.

104
00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.000
- Dennis!
- Dennis!

105
00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:52.000
Tinkles was crying,
so we let him out.

106
00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.000
Ahhh!

107
00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.000
Tinkles, sit!

108
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:12.000
Ah. Whose idea was it
to let Dennis have a puppy?

109
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:16.000
Um... Yours?

110
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.000
Right.

111
00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.000
Poor Tinkles.

112
00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.000
Dennis...

113
00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.000
Look, honey,
I know you love Tinkles,

114
00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.000
but we're not allowed
to bring our dogs...

115
00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:29.000
Uh... I mean, our pets everywhere.

116
00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.000
Okay?

117
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.000
Okay.

118
00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:39.000
DJ Jazzy Johnny in the house.

119
00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:43.000
It's time to welcome the happy
couple, Mr. and Mrs. Prickles!

120
00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:47.000
Aw!

121
00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.000
The bride and groom
invite everyone

122
00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:53.000
to join them
on the dance floor.

123
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.000
Care to dance?

124
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.000
Is that her?

125
00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.000
Ooh! Watch out now.

126
00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:07.000
She got stitches
in all the right places.

127
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.000
Okay, there's no way that
is related to you, Frank.

128
00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.000
No, she's
my right arm's cousin.

129
00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.000
Ay! Oh!

130
00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:18.000
- Oh!
- Ah! I see it now.

131
00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.000
Frank wanted me to meet you.

132
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:24.000
We're arm cousins,
twice removed.

133
00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.000
Of course.

134
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:30.000
I'd recognize that bicep
anywhere.

135
00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.000
He thought, since we're both
single, we might hit it off,

136
00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.000
maybe go on a date?

137
00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:36.000
"Date"? Oh!

138
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:39.000
Well, eh,
it's just that, eh...

139
00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.000
Whoa!

140
00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.000
The DJ booth
is a sacred space!

141
00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.000
I love this song!

142
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.000
Don't you?

143
00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.000
Dracula?

144
00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.000
Oh, where'd he go?

145
00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:57.000
Dracula?

146
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.000
What's the matter, Drac,
you didn't like her?

147
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.000
No offense, but you
can't be too picky.

148
00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:06.000
You haven't had a date
in 100 years.

149
00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:10.000
Look, guys, I appreciate your
concern, but it's not up to me.

150
00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:14.000
You only Zing once,
and I did.

151
00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.000
Times have changed, buddy.

152
00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.000
You can even find someone to
Zing with on your phone now.

153
00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:20.000
What? Really?

154
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.000
Oh. Oh, no, no, no.

155
00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.000
I'm far too busy.

156
00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:27.000
I have Mavis and Dennis and the
hotel, and bleh, bleh-bleh.

157
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.000
Um, did you guys
hear that?

158
00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.000
He actually said,
"Bleh, bleh-bleh."

159
00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:35.000
I don't say,
"Bleh, bleh-bleh"!

160
00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:45.000
Eh, uh,
I'm looking for a Zing.

161
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.000
Okay. Changing phone ring.

162
00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:53.000
No, no.
I'm looking for a date.

163
00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.000
No, no, no.

164
00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:58.000
I want to meet someone.

165
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.000
Are you kidding me right now?

166
00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:06.000
Don't you get it?
I want to go on a date!

167
00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.000
I'm lonely.

168
00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:14.000
You want baloney.

169
00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.000
What? Look at
that hair. Come on.

170
00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:22.000
Ah. Too many eyes.

171
00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:24.000
Too few eyes.

172
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.000
Not into tentacles.

173
00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.000
"Match found"?

174
00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:29.000
No, no, no!

175
00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:30.000
First things first.

176
00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.000
Whoa!

177
00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.000
I'm not into games.

178
00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:36.000
You'd better have a job,
and my cats have to like you.

179
00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.000
Oh, no.

180
00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:40.000
Oh, whoa, no.

181
00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.000
Dad?

182
00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.000
Oh! Mavis! Oh.

183
00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.000
Uh, what are you doing here?

184
00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:48.000
I was just checking on the honeymoon
suite, and I heard something.

185
00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.000
Oh, I'm sorry,
my little bedbug.

186
00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:53.000
I was just cleaning
the attic.

187
00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.000
It's so dirty, ah, yes...

188
00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.000
- Who is that?
- Are you on the phone?

189
00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:07.000
What, this? I was just
trying to find a maid

190
00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:09.000
- to help me with the mess.
- A maid?

191
00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.000
Who do you think...

192
00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:12.000
Thank you,
I'll check your references

193
00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.000
and get back to you. Goodbye!

194
00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:19.000
Dad.

195
00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:20.000
Stop trying to
hide it from me.

196
00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:23.000
Hide? Who?
I mean, what? Me?

197
00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.000
Yes.

198
00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.000
And I know what it is.

199
00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.000
Uh... Really?

200
00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:31.000
You're stressed out
from working too hard.

201
00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.000
Oh!

202
00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.000
Okay, yes.

203
00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.000
You got me.

204
00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.000
It's a big hotel,
you know?

205
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:38.000
Can't get to everything.

206
00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:40.000
But what about you?

207
00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:42.000
You're pretty busy yourself.

208
00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.000
I know. It seems like now that
we're working together more,

209
00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.000
we're seeing
each other less.

210
00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:50.000
Ah. Yeah.
You're absolutely right.

211
00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:53.000
I am working too much,
you're working too much.

212
00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:56.000
We should really take a break,
starting right now.

213
00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:58.000
Night-night.

214
00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.000
I'm still here!

215
00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:18.000
Aw.

216
00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.000
Oh! Hey, honey.

217
00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:23.000
You ready for

218
00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:25.000
date night?

219
00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:26.000
Aw.

220
00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:27.000
That's okay, sweetheart.

221
00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:30.000
You rest.

222
00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:34.000
You know, Dad's right.

223
00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.000
We need a break.

224
00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.000
We need to all be together
again, like a family.

225
00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:41.000
Like we used to.

226
00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:46.000
Are you
overworked and stressed out?

227
00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:48.000
Do you need some family time?

228
00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:50.000
Are you a monster?

229
00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:52.000
Then you need a vacation,

230
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:56.000
a monster vacation.

231
00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:03.000
Welcome aboard
Gremlin Air.

232
00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:10.000
Ah!

233
00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.000
Ladies and gentlemen,

234
00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.000
please direct your attention
to the front of the cabin.

235
00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:26.000
For your safety, please
unbuckle your seat belts.

236
00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:28.000
Ooh.

237
00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:33.000
In the likely event we experience
a sudden drop in cabin pressure,

238
00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:36.000
oxygen will be provided.

239
00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.000
Can I stow that
for you, sir?

240
00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:41.000
All right. Thanks.

241
00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:45.000
Beverages. Snacks. Beverages.

242
00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:46.000
Beverages. Snacks.

243
00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:49.000
Beverages.

244
00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.000
Ahhh!

245
00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:56.000
- Coffee?
- That would be lovely.

246
00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:04.000
Mavis, please,
you're torturing me.

247
00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:07.000
You know I hate surprises.

248
00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:09.000
This is
a fun surprise.

249
00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:11.000
There are no fun surprises.

250
00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.000
Just tell me
where we're going.

251
00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.000
Why are we on a plane?

252
00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.000
We can fly, you know.

253
00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:19.000
Back in my day,
people took trains.

254
00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.000
Now, that's classy.

255
00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:23.000
Sure, Dad. Forty hours
in a closet-sized room

256
00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:26.000
with you and Uncle Bernie
and his smelly cigars,

257
00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:28.000
arguing who was
more attractive,

258
00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:30.000
Cleopatra or Nefertiti.

259
00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.000
Nefertiti.

260
00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:34.000
Okay, Dad, thank you.

261
00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:37.000
Mavis, this is
such an amazing surprise!

262
00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:41.000
I can't wait to spend time
with the people I love most.

263
00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:45.000
But I beg of you,
tell me where we're going!

264
00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:49.000
Nope. I've taken care of everything,
so you don't need to worry.

265
00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:50.000
You've been
so stressed out lately.

266
00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:54.000
It's time for you to relax.

267
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.000
Now, isn't that better?

268
00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:04.000
Oh, yes.

269
00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.000
So relaxed.

270
00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:11.000
I'm gonna go check
on you-know-who.

271
00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:12.000
I'll be right back.

272
00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:15.000
I have to go to the bathroom.

273
00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:16.000
Hey, did you see that?

274
00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:17.000
Dennis went to the bathroom!

275
00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:20.000
Uh... Okay.

276
00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:26.000
Psst. Hey, where are you?

277
00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.000
There you are, Tinkles.

278
00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:35.000
Don't worry, we'd never
leave you home alone.

279
00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.000
Okay, folks,
you're free to move

280
00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.000
about the cabin, as we have

281
00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.000
started our descent.

282
00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:57.000
So, any big plans
for the weekend there, Bill?

283
00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.000
Oh, you know,
the usual.

284
00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:01.000
Got to take the kids
to soccer.

285
00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:06.000
Snacks. Beverages.

286
00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:09.000
Snacks. Beverages. Snacks.

287
00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.000
Ladies and gentlemen, we've
arrived at our destination,

288
00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:26.000
the Bermuda Triangle.

289
00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:40.000
Ooh!

290
00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:18.000
Welcome to
the Bermuda Triangle,

291
00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:23.000
where you'll embark on a
monster cruise of a lifetime.

292
00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:27.000
A cruise?

293
00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:29.000
Surprise!

294
00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:31.000
Oh, no, you... No.

295
00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:35.000
But it's just like a hotel
on the water.

296
00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:37.000
I just figured
you need a vacation

297
00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:40.000
from running
everyone else's vacation.

298
00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:43.000
You've barely been
out of the hotel since...

299
00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:46.000
Well, since Mom died.

300
00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.000
But this is a chance
to make new memories,

301
00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.000
with all of us.

302
00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:52.000
With Dennis.

303
00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:58.000
- Boat!
- Boat!

304
00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:03.000
Who made you
such an amazing daughter?

305
00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.000
You.

306
00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:06.000
That's right!

307
00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:08.000
What a father I am.

308
00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:11.000
Come on, Denisovich,
let's get cruising!

309
00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.000
Yay!

310
00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:35.000
Wow!

311
00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:02.000
Okay. Smile.

312
00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:04.000
Thank you.

313
00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:15.000
Ow!

314
00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.000
"No pets allowed"?

315
00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:19.000
Uh-oh.

316
00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:30.000
Perfect.

317
00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:37.000
Welcome aboard.
How are you doing?

318
00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:39.000
- Dennis, come on.
- Nice to see you.

319
00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:40.000
Oh, lovely shirt. Yes.

320
00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:44.000
Oh, hello.
Welcome aboard.

321
00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:53.000
Uh, this is Bob.

322
00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:54.000
Say hi, Bob.

323
00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.000
"Hi, Bob."

324
00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:05.000
Oh, my gosh, Griffin.

325
00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:07.000
I'm, like, so excited.

326
00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:10.000
This is, like, the nicest
hotel I've ever been to.

327
00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:11.000
Yeah!

328
00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:13.000
Man, this is amazing!

329
00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.000
There's so much to do!

330
00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:17.000
Olympic-size swimming pool...

331
00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:20.000
All-you-can-eat buffet...

332
00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:25.000
Full-service spa...

333
00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:28.000
Whoo! I'm gonna get me
a seaweed rewrap!

334
00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:31.000
Wow, it sounds like
everything we can do

335
00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.000
at our hotel!

336
00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:36.000
Except on the water!

337
00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:49.000
Ooh! Ah!

338
00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:51.000
Wow!

339
00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.000
You nailed it, honey.

340
00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:55.000
Your dad is going to
love this!

341
00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:57.000
Best summer vacation ever!

342
00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:58.000
Wait till you see
the itinerary.

343
00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:00.000
Oh!

344
00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.000
That's nice.

345
00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:04.000
Frank, "fire bad." Remember?

346
00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:07.000
Oh, yeah, right, but,
uh, maybe you'll find

347
00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:09.000
your own fireworks
on the cruise, huh?

348
00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.000
It's not the Love Boat, Frank.

349
00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:15.000
I'm just here to have fun
with my family.

350
00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:20.000
Huh?

351
00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:22.000
Ha!

352
00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:24.000
Ahoy there!

353
00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:26.000
Welcome aboard!

354
00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:36.000
Whoa! Who is that?

355
00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:42.000
I am Captain Ericka.

356
00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:45.000
And, yes, I'm human. But
don't hold that against me.

357
00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:48.000
I could not be more excited
to have all of you on board

358
00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:52.000
our first-ever
monster cruise!

359
00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:59.000
Whoo-hoo!

360
00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.000
Dad? Are you okay?

361
00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:04.000
Eeny feeny fanny
foonyah wah wah?

362
00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:06.000
Oh, no! He's having
a heart attack!

363
00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:08.000
Drac? Not likely.

364
00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:10.000
Yeah, the only heart attack that can
hurt him is with a wooden stake.

365
00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:11.000
It must be a stroke!

366
00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:13.000
Actually, I think
it might be her.

367
00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:16.000
Ow! Watch where you're pointing,
mister, I'm right here.

368
00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:18.000
You always stand
so close to me.

369
00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:20.000
It's creepy.

370
00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:23.000
For so long, monsters were
hiding, living in the shadows,

371
00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:25.000
but not anymore!

372
00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:29.000
You've stood up and waved
your hand or claw or tentacle

373
00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:35.000
and said, "We're here, we're hairy,
and it is our right to be scary!"

374
00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:40.000
Now it's time to celebrate!

375
00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:43.000
You'll enjoy gourmet dining,
thrilling adventures,

376
00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:45.000
and nonstop entertainment,

377
00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:48.000
all on the way
to our final destination,

378
00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:51.000
the lost city
that isn't lost anymore,

379
00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:54.000
Atlantis!

380
00:22:58.000 --> 00:22:59.000
Oh, yeah!

381
00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:01.000
Whoo-hoo!

382
00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:03.000
Whoa!
The fish are acrobats!

383
00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:06.000
They're fishcrobats!

384
00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:10.000
Hello. How y'all doing?

385
00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:12.000
So...

386
00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:17.000
You must be
the one and only Dracula.

387
00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:21.000
I have waited so long
to meet you.

388
00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:23.000
Wow, you really don't age,
do you?

389
00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:25.000
I would kill
for your skin.

390
00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:28.000
Eh doobeeday
shoolah eh koobeeday?

391
00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:30.000
Oh. You're speaking
Transylvanian.

392
00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.000
Oh. Always wanted
to learn.

393
00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:34.000
Uh, eh doobeeday
shoolah koobeeday?

394
00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:38.000
- Eh koobeeday.
- Koobeeday.

395
00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:41.000
Eh doobeeday
shoolah koobeeday.

396
00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:43.000
Doolah-day shoolah koobeeday.

397
00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:46.000
Oh, such a romantic language.

398
00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:47.000
You know, there's just
something about an accent

399
00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:51.000
that makes a man
sound so intelligent.

400
00:23:51.000 --> 00:23:52.000
Alibooboo.

401
00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:54.000
That's Transylvanian
right there.

402
00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:56.000
He's saying
it's nice to meet you.

403
00:23:56.000 --> 00:24:00.000
Well, then
"alibooboo" to you as well.

404
00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.000
- Alibooboo. Alibooboo.
- Drac! Drac, snap out of it.

405
00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:05.000
Wait. I've always wanted
to do this.

406
00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:07.000
Wake up! Wake up, Drac!

407
00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:09.000
Snap out of it!

408
00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:10.000
Hey, cut it out!

409
00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:12.000
Hey, buddy, you okay?

410
00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:14.000
No, not okay.

411
00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:16.000
Not okay!

412
00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:18.000
I... I...

413
00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:19.000
I...

414
00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:22.000
Zinged.

415
00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:12.000
Mmm!

416
00:25:13.000 --> 00:25:14.000
- Ooh!
- Oh!

417
00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:16.000
Check that out!

418
00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:20.000
Ah!

419
00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:24.000
Here we go.

420
00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:26.000
Mmm, yummy.

421
00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:39.000
Ah!

422
00:25:57.000 --> 00:25:59.000
Papa.

423
00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:14.000
"Kids Club."

424
00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:16.000
What's a kids club?

425
00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:25.000
Whee!

426
00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:29.000
- Fish.
- That's right, dear.

427
00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:30.000
I'm still not sure
I understand.

428
00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:34.000
You take my kids,
all day, on purpose?

429
00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:35.000
Fish.

430
00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:37.000
That's right.

431
00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:39.000
What exactly
don't you understand?

432
00:26:39.000 --> 00:26:41.000
- Why? Ow!
- Shh.

433
00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:44.000
So they can have a great time,
and you can have a great time.

434
00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:47.000
Fish.

435
00:26:47.000 --> 00:26:51.000
Oh, don't worry, you get them
back at the end of the day.

436
00:26:51.000 --> 00:26:53.000
Fish.

437
00:26:53.000 --> 00:26:56.000
Oh, well. That's better
than nothing.

438
00:26:57.000 --> 00:26:59.000
Oh. Oh!

439
00:27:05.000 --> 00:27:06.000
So...

440
00:27:06.000 --> 00:27:07.000
What do we do now?

441
00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:13.000
I think we do
whatever we want.

442
00:27:13.000 --> 00:27:15.000
"Whatever we want"?

443
00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:18.000
Whatever we want.

444
00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:20.000
Whatever we want!

445
00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:24.000
Whatever we want.

446
00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:26.000
- Stop! Help me!
- Whatever we want.

447
00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:30.000
- Whatever we want.
- Whatever we want.

448
00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:31.000
Oh, hi. Hello.

449
00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:33.000
How y'all doin'?

450
00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:34.000
- Oh.
- Good evening, Captain.

451
00:27:34.000 --> 00:27:36.000
Well, hello.
Oh, my goodness.

452
00:27:36.000 --> 00:27:38.000
Ah!

453
00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:41.000
Would you mind, uh, lifting your tail?
You know...

454
00:27:41.000 --> 00:27:43.000
Oh! Certainly.

455
00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:46.000
Okay. Thank you
so much.

456
00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:49.000
Oh, hello.

457
00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:51.000
Welcome aboard.

458
00:28:17.000 --> 00:28:21.000
Ugh! You were so right,
Great-Grandfather.

459
00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:24.000
Monsters are disgusting!

460
00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:27.000
They're animals!

461
00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:46.000
I'll be right there.

462
00:28:52.000 --> 00:28:55.000
Dracula, is he on board?

463
00:28:55.000 --> 00:28:58.000
Yes. I saw him.
Face-to-face. Ugh!

464
00:28:58.000 --> 00:29:00.000
I was so nice to him.

465
00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:02.000
That pale face of his
and his goofy smile,

466
00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:04.000
showing off his fangs.

467
00:29:04.000 --> 00:29:06.000
Argh, it's just like
you taught me!

468
00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:08.000
It's even worse than I feared!

469
00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:11.000
It was that fateful night
that I realized

470
00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:16.000
a human could never defeat
a monster.

471
00:29:19.000 --> 00:29:23.000
But I wouldn't let
our family legacy die.

472
00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:28.000
And so, I began to search
for an answer.

473
00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:33.000
And I saw it in an ancient text,
an instrument of destruction

474
00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:36.000
so powerful
it destroyed Atlantis,

475
00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:40.000
a whole city of monsters.

476
00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:44.000
And there, deep within the
rubble, it lay, waiting.

477
00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:48.000
Endlessly, I searched
for the lost city

478
00:29:48.000 --> 00:29:51.000
Time passed, and my body
began to fail me.

479
00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:54.000
Oh, it was so sad, Ericka.

480
00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:56.000
First my liver,
then my spleen,

481
00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:59.000
followed by a kidney or two.

482
00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:03.000
Then my golden locks.

483
00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:05.000
But I wouldn't let
that stop me.

484
00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:10.000
I replaced my failing organs
with technology!

485
00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:12.000
Ha-ha!

486
00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:14.000
And look at me now.

487
00:30:14.000 --> 00:30:15.000
Mmm-hmm!

488
00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:19.000
Oh, girl,
it's an improvement, really.

489
00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:22.000
Um, sure.

490
00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:27.000
And now, after 120 years,
I have finally found Atlantis.

491
00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:29.000
Oh, forget about all this!

492
00:30:29.000 --> 00:30:31.000
Let me get rid of
Dracula right now.

493
00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:33.000
I was so close to him,
I could've just...

494
00:30:34.000 --> 00:30:37.000
No, no, no!

495
00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:39.000
We have to
stick to the plan.

496
00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:41.000
Lure the monsters
to Atlantis,

497
00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:43.000
retrieve the instrument
of destruction,

498
00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:46.000
trap them there,
and then wipe them out.

499
00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:48.000
It's simple, Ericka!

500
00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:51.000
Now, promise me you won't
try and kill Dracula.

501
00:30:51.000 --> 00:30:52.000
Ugh, fine!

502
00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:55.000
- I promise.
- Promise what?

503
00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:59.000
I promise I won't
try and kill Dracula. Okay?

504
00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:05.000
Ugh.

505
00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:09.000
Don't worry, Great-Grandfather,
I won't try and kill him...

506
00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:12.000
I will kill him.

507
00:31:37.000 --> 00:31:40.000
Whew!

508
00:32:13.000 --> 00:32:16.000
Ugh!

509
00:32:23.000 --> 00:32:25.000
Oh!

510
00:32:52.000 --> 00:32:54.000
Work it, Dracula.

511
00:32:54.000 --> 00:32:57.000
You know it.

512
00:32:57.000 --> 00:33:00.000
Oh! Lookin' good, Drac!

513
00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:01.000
Feeling good, Frank.

514
00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:04.000
Look at you, so fancy!

515
00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:05.000
What? This? Please.

516
00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:07.000
Ooh! Dressed to impress, huh?

517
00:33:07.000 --> 00:33:09.000
"Impress"? Oh.

518
00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:11.000
Who do I need to impress?

519
00:33:11.000 --> 00:33:13.000
Hey, isn't that
Captain Ericka?

520
00:33:13.000 --> 00:33:14.000
Oh, no!

521
00:33:14.000 --> 00:33:17.000
Uh, what? Eh, oh...

522
00:33:17.000 --> 00:33:19.000
Oops, no,
not her.

523
00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:21.000
Ooh, that's good!

524
00:33:21.000 --> 00:33:24.000
Very amusing.

525
00:33:32.000 --> 00:33:35.000
Sorry, Drac. You know, it's just
we've never seen you like this.

526
00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:36.000
I know.

527
00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:37.000
It doesn't make any sense.

528
00:33:37.000 --> 00:33:40.000
You can't Zing twice,
it's impossible!

529
00:33:40.000 --> 00:33:42.000
But I did! So now what?

530
00:33:42.000 --> 00:33:45.000
And what about Mavis?

531
00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:47.000
She wants you
to be happy, right?

532
00:33:47.000 --> 00:33:50.000
I'm sure she'll go
with the flow.

533
00:33:50.000 --> 00:33:52.000
Oh, no, no, no!

534
00:33:52.000 --> 00:33:54.000
Mavis needs me.
She depends on me.

535
00:33:54.000 --> 00:33:57.000
I need to be home
with my family.

536
00:33:57.000 --> 00:34:02.000
Hey, Murray here may be from
Egypt, but you're the one in

537
00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:04.000
"da Nile."

538
00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:06.000
You guys get that?

539
00:34:06.000 --> 00:34:07.000
Ow! You hit me right in the...

540
00:34:07.000 --> 00:34:09.000
Mavis!

541
00:34:12.000 --> 00:34:15.000
Don't say a word, or
I'll haunt your dreams.

542
00:34:16.000 --> 00:34:18.000
Having fun?

543
00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:20.000
Oh, I'm having even more fun
now that you're here.

544
00:34:20.000 --> 00:34:24.000
You know, Dad, I feel really lucky
to have this time with you.

545
00:34:24.000 --> 00:34:27.000
All of us together,
it's really special.

546
00:34:27.000 --> 00:34:30.000
Me, too,
spider monkey.

547
00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:33.000
Now, are you ready for me to
destroy you in monster ball?

548
00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:36.000
Whoo-hoo! Monster ball!

549
00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:37.000
Come on, Papa Drac!

550
00:34:37.000 --> 00:34:39.000
Bring it on!

551
00:34:39.000 --> 00:34:43.000
For I am king of family fun!

552
00:34:44.000 --> 00:34:49.000
Ha-ha! All right!
Who is ready to get pummeled?

553
00:34:50.000 --> 00:34:52.000
I got to warn you,

554
00:34:52.000 --> 00:34:55.000
I played second-team coed intramural
volleyball at Santa Cruz.

555
00:34:55.000 --> 00:34:58.000
Sure, pal. Whatever you say.

556
00:34:58.000 --> 00:35:00.000
Everybody, just please
watch the hair.

557
00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.000
Watch the hair!

558
00:35:02.000 --> 00:35:05.000
Oh-ho-ho! Let's go!
Let's do this!

559
00:35:05.000 --> 00:35:07.000
Oh, my gosh, this is
gonna be so much fun.

560
00:35:07.000 --> 00:35:08.000
Ha-ha! Get ready.

561
00:35:08.000 --> 00:35:11.000
Here comes the pain!

562
00:35:14.000 --> 00:35:16.000
- Spike!
- Not the hair!

563
00:35:16.000 --> 00:35:19.000
Whoa!

564
00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:23.000
No, no, no!

565
00:35:24.000 --> 00:35:26.000
All right!

566
00:35:26.000 --> 00:35:30.000
Captain
Ericka, you are needed on deck.

567
00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:33.000
Next stop...
Buh-bye, Dracula.

568
00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:36.000
Ha-ha! All right, baby!

569
00:35:57.000 --> 00:35:58.000
Oh, baby, I got this.

570
00:35:58.000 --> 00:36:00.000
Hey there, monsters.

571
00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:02.000
Huh?

572
00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:06.000
Yeah! What'd I say!

573
00:36:08.000 --> 00:36:12.000
We're arriving
at our first destination.

574
00:36:16.000 --> 00:36:19.000
The underwater volcano!

575
00:36:19.000 --> 00:36:23.000
Everyone, grab your scuba
gear and get ready to explore

576
00:36:23.000 --> 00:36:26.000
the wonders of the sea.

577
00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:28.000
Especially you,

578
00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:31.000
Count Dracula.

579
00:36:34.000 --> 00:36:36.000
You see that, pal?
She likes you.

580
00:36:36.000 --> 00:36:37.000
Oh, no, no, no.

581
00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:39.000
That sounds like a Zing
in full effect.

582
00:36:39.000 --> 00:36:41.000
Oh, no, no, no.

583
00:36:41.000 --> 00:36:43.000
Oh, yes, yes, yes.

584
00:36:43.000 --> 00:36:46.000
I'm just here
to have family fun.

585
00:36:46.000 --> 00:36:49.000
Family, family, fun, fun.

586
00:37:10.000 --> 00:37:13.000
Hmm, let's see.
What about here?

587
00:37:33.000 --> 00:37:36.000
Right this way, everyone.

588
00:37:47.000 --> 00:37:51.000
Welcome to one of the true wonders
of the underwater kingdom.

589
00:37:51.000 --> 00:37:54.000
I give you Volcano del Fuego.

590
00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:57.000
Or, as the local sea life
call it...

591
00:38:56.000 --> 00:38:59.000
Whee!

592
00:39:53.000 --> 00:39:54.000
Aw, what a cute family.

593
00:39:54.000 --> 00:39:55.000
What? No, it's not.

594
00:39:55.000 --> 00:39:58.000
Argh! Dracula bad!

595
00:41:12.000 --> 00:41:14.000
Frank, we just ate.

596
00:41:14.000 --> 00:41:16.000
I can't believe
you're hungry already.

597
00:41:16.000 --> 00:41:18.000
I'm sorry.
You know what it is?

598
00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:19.000
It's all... Just all that
seafood just swimming around,

599
00:41:19.000 --> 00:41:21.000
and when I "see food..."

600
00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:25.000
Oh, man! I'm gone.

601
00:41:25.000 --> 00:41:27.000
Oh! Dracula, Dracula, Dracula!

602
00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:30.000
Dracula, Dracula!

603
00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:33.000
I get so close, but it's
almost like he's teasing me.

604
00:41:33.000 --> 00:41:35.000
I just, I can't
stand it anymore.

605
00:41:35.000 --> 00:41:37.000
I have to get him!

606
00:41:47.000 --> 00:41:50.000
Boy, that underwater volcano
looked hot.

607
00:41:50.000 --> 00:41:53.000
Mmm-hmm.

608
00:41:56.000 --> 00:41:58.000
Oh... Hi, Bob.

609
00:41:58.000 --> 00:42:02.000
Right. We promised you we'd
play, uh, ping-pong now.

610
00:42:02.000 --> 00:42:04.000
Um, Dennis?
Who is this?

611
00:42:04.000 --> 00:42:06.000
Uh, it's our friend, Bob.

612
00:42:06.000 --> 00:42:09.000
- Say hi, Bob.
- "Hi, Bob."

613
00:42:10.000 --> 00:42:13.000
Okay! Time to go
play ping-pong.

614
00:42:13.000 --> 00:42:18.000
- Drac!
- Drac!

615
00:42:18.000 --> 00:42:21.000
Hey, boys,
where's the fire?

616
00:42:21.000 --> 00:42:22.000
Oh, well,
Griffin here, he...

617
00:42:22.000 --> 00:42:24.000
- He has something to tell you.
- Me? Uh...

618
00:42:24.000 --> 00:42:27.000
Oh. Yeah, I got this bite on
my hand, and since, you know,

619
00:42:27.000 --> 00:42:29.000
you're a biting expert, I
thought you could take a look.

620
00:42:29.000 --> 00:42:32.000
- Yeah. Come on over here.
- The light is better.

621
00:42:32.000 --> 00:42:34.000
Okay...

622
00:42:35.000 --> 00:42:37.000
Okay, what is going on?

623
00:42:37.000 --> 00:42:40.000
You guys are acting weirder than normal,
and your normal is pretty weird.

624
00:42:40.000 --> 00:42:43.000
You are not gonna believe
what we heard, but...

625
00:42:57.000 --> 00:42:59.000
Shh. I told you I don't
want to upset Mavis.

626
00:42:59.000 --> 00:43:02.000
But what are you talking about?

627
00:43:02.000 --> 00:43:04.000
Okay, well, see, Frank got
hungry, so no surprise there...

628
00:43:04.000 --> 00:43:08.000
But we swam back to the ship, and
we found Ericka raving about you.

629
00:43:08.000 --> 00:43:10.000
She can't live
without you, buddy.

630
00:43:10.000 --> 00:43:12.000
It's serious!

631
00:43:15.000 --> 00:43:19.000
So, Drac, this is great. Are you gonna
make a move on the captain, or what?

632
00:43:19.000 --> 00:43:20.000
Uh, yes.

633
00:43:20.000 --> 00:43:23.000
- Maybe? No.
- Ugh.

634
00:43:23.000 --> 00:43:26.000
It's been a while. I don't
even know where to start.

635
00:43:26.000 --> 00:43:29.000
It's easy, Drac.
Just make some small talk.

636
00:43:29.000 --> 00:43:31.000
- Remember to smile.
- Look into her eyes.

637
00:43:31.000 --> 00:43:33.000
- Keep it casual.
- Say something funny.

638
00:43:33.000 --> 00:43:34.000
Ask her where
her parts are from.

639
00:43:34.000 --> 00:43:36.000
Oh, and say
that her wrappings look nice.

640
00:43:36.000 --> 00:43:37.000
- "Do you like coffins?"
- Compliment her.

641
00:43:37.000 --> 00:43:39.000
- "Your neck looks delicious."
- Here she comes.

642
00:43:39.000 --> 00:43:42.000
Okay, Drac,
hit it.

643
00:43:42.000 --> 00:43:44.000
Your delicious neck wrappings
are in a nice coffin.

644
00:43:44.000 --> 00:43:48.000
Would you like
to see my parts?

645
00:43:50.000 --> 00:43:52.000
Yes, I'd love to go out
with you.

646
00:43:52.000 --> 00:43:53.000
Ay! What?

647
00:43:53.000 --> 00:43:54.000
What?

648
00:43:54.000 --> 00:43:56.000
Cantina. Midnight.

649
00:43:56.000 --> 00:43:58.000
Don't be late.

650
00:44:06.000 --> 00:44:08.000
Whew!

651
00:44:08.000 --> 00:44:10.000
That was a close one.

652
00:44:13.000 --> 00:44:16.000
- Wait! Stop it, Tinkles, stop!
- Wait, Tinkles. Come back.

653
00:44:25.000 --> 00:44:27.000
- Tinkles, stop!
- Wait!

654
00:44:27.000 --> 00:44:29.000
No, no, no!

655
00:44:41.000 --> 00:44:42.000
Tinkles, stop!

656
00:44:42.000 --> 00:44:45.000
I've been found!

657
00:44:45.000 --> 00:44:48.000
You'll never get me, monster!

658
00:44:48.000 --> 00:44:51.000
Shh! Tinkles, stop.
Shh! Shh!

659
00:45:04.000 --> 00:45:06.000
Ew.

660
00:45:14.000 --> 00:45:20.000
Everybody, we are pulling up
to our next stop, the Deserted Island.

661
00:45:20.000 --> 00:45:22.000
It's time to get lost
on the beach,

662
00:45:22.000 --> 00:45:29.000
and we hope you'll find yourself
some fun and relaxation.

663
00:45:29.000 --> 00:45:31.000
Whoo-hoo!
Beach time!

664
00:45:31.000 --> 00:45:33.000
Johnny, you go
set everything up.

665
00:45:33.000 --> 00:45:35.000
And, Dad, you go get in
line for the snow cones.

666
00:45:35.000 --> 00:45:38.000
You know, actually,
I was thinking you and Johnny

667
00:45:38.000 --> 00:45:40.000
should spend
some time together.

668
00:45:40.000 --> 00:45:42.000
What do you call it again?
Eh, date night?

669
00:45:42.000 --> 00:45:43.000
Date night?

670
00:45:43.000 --> 00:45:45.000
- What are you gonna do?
- Well, I thought

671
00:45:45.000 --> 00:45:48.000
me and the guys would
take this opportunity

672
00:45:48.000 --> 00:45:51.000
to spend some quality time
with Dennis.

673
00:45:51.000 --> 00:45:53.000
Oh. Okay.
That's a great idea.

674
00:45:53.000 --> 00:45:54.000
Come on, Johnny.
Date night.

675
00:45:54.000 --> 00:45:58.000
Duh-duh-duh-duh-date night!

676
00:46:12.000 --> 00:46:15.000
Okay, here you go!

677
00:46:19.000 --> 00:46:22.000
- Good girl!
- I got this one.

678
00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:31.000
What was that?

679
00:46:31.000 --> 00:46:33.000
It sounds like our children.

680
00:46:33.000 --> 00:46:36.000
- It is our children! Run!
- Run!

681
00:46:36.000 --> 00:46:38.000
Please! Help! Someone!

682
00:46:38.000 --> 00:46:40.000
Get the parents!

683
00:46:40.000 --> 00:46:43.000
Frank? Would you rub
some moonscreen on my back

684
00:46:43.000 --> 00:46:45.000
before I get burned?

685
00:46:45.000 --> 00:46:46.000
Wait one second, honey.

686
00:46:46.000 --> 00:46:48.000
You know, the kids buried me
in the sand.

687
00:46:54.000 --> 00:46:55.000
Mmm. Thanks, honey.

688
00:46:55.000 --> 00:46:58.000
- Shall we have another?
- Sure.

689
00:46:58.000 --> 00:47:01.000
- Sounds good.
- Straight up.

690
00:47:01.000 --> 00:47:03.000
Isn't this place amazing?

691
00:47:03.000 --> 00:47:06.000
Whoa! The menu is in a bottle!

692
00:47:06.000 --> 00:47:09.000
Genius! Isn't that
awesome, honey?

693
00:47:11.000 --> 00:47:12.000
What? Oh, sorry.

694
00:47:12.000 --> 00:47:14.000
I was just thinking
about my dad.

695
00:47:14.000 --> 00:47:17.000
Don't you think
he's acting weird lately?

696
00:47:17.000 --> 00:47:21.000
Not really. Besides having
a huge crush on the captain.

697
00:47:21.000 --> 00:47:23.000
- What?
- Oh, yeah.

698
00:47:23.000 --> 00:47:25.000
The Love Boat is definitely
making another run.

699
00:47:25.000 --> 00:47:27.000
No way. He's...

700
00:47:27.000 --> 00:47:29.000
He's my dad.

701
00:47:29.000 --> 00:47:31.000
I know, right? It's weird.

702
00:47:31.000 --> 00:47:35.000
When my parents kiss,
I still close my eyes.

703
00:47:35.000 --> 00:47:40.000
I guess I never thought about
him with anyone besides my mom.

704
00:47:40.000 --> 00:47:43.000
You're cool with it,
though, right?

705
00:47:43.000 --> 00:47:45.000
Of course. I want him
to be happy.

706
00:47:45.000 --> 00:47:47.000
Totally.

707
00:47:48.000 --> 00:47:51.000
Totally.

708
00:47:56.000 --> 00:47:58.000
Buenas noches, mi amigo.

709
00:47:58.000 --> 00:48:04.000
Have you a beverage
to quench me of my parchment?

710
00:48:04.000 --> 00:48:08.000
Yes, of course,
Mr. Chupacabra.

711
00:48:11.000 --> 00:48:14.000
Muchas gracias.

712
00:48:29.000 --> 00:48:30.000
You look ravishing.

713
00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:31.000
Oh.

714
00:48:31.000 --> 00:48:32.000
Uh, thank you. I just...

715
00:48:32.000 --> 00:48:35.000
Oh.

716
00:48:43.000 --> 00:48:45.000
So, um...

717
00:48:45.000 --> 00:48:48.000
Does Captain Ericka
have a last name?

718
00:48:48.000 --> 00:48:49.000
Uh, oh, uh...

719
00:48:49.000 --> 00:48:51.000
Oh, guacamole!

720
00:48:51.000 --> 00:48:53.000
"Ericka Guacamole"?

721
00:48:53.000 --> 00:48:56.000
That's so international.

722
00:48:56.000 --> 00:49:00.000
No.
Guacamole for us to share.

723
00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:02.000
Oh, how beautiful
is that full moon tonight?

724
00:49:02.000 --> 00:49:05.000
Look. Right behind you.

725
00:49:08.000 --> 00:49:13.000
Mmm! The food here
is to die for.

726
00:49:22.000 --> 00:49:26.000
Holy moly, that was
a lot of guacamole.

727
00:49:26.000 --> 00:49:29.000
Are you feeling all right?

728
00:49:29.000 --> 00:49:32.000
- Totally fine. Why?
- No reason.

729
00:49:33.000 --> 00:49:35.000
Oh...

730
00:49:35.000 --> 00:49:38.000
There must have been garlic
in the guacamole.

731
00:49:38.000 --> 00:49:40.000
Oh, no.

732
00:49:40.000 --> 00:49:41.000
Isn't that deadly
for you?

733
00:49:41.000 --> 00:49:44.000
No, no, no.
It's just that I'm...

734
00:49:44.000 --> 00:49:47.000
Garlic intolerant.

735
00:49:54.000 --> 00:49:56.000
Was that you?

736
00:49:57.000 --> 00:50:00.000
Whoo!

737
00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:01.000
Oh, yeah!

738
00:50:01.000 --> 00:50:04.000
Dolphin surfing!

739
00:50:11.000 --> 00:50:12.000
Whoa!

740
00:50:12.000 --> 00:50:14.000
Hi, Mama. Hi, Papa.

741
00:50:14.000 --> 00:50:15.000
Hey-hey.

742
00:50:15.000 --> 00:50:17.000
Oh! Hey there.

743
00:50:17.000 --> 00:50:19.000
- Papa.
- Hidey-ho!

744
00:50:19.000 --> 00:50:20.000
Hi.

745
00:50:20.000 --> 00:50:24.000
Is my dad
in there, too?

746
00:50:25.000 --> 00:50:27.000
Don't worry,
I'm over here. Bleh, bleh-bleh.

747
00:50:27.000 --> 00:50:32.000
No, Papa Drac's not here.
He's on his date.

748
00:50:32.000 --> 00:50:34.000
Date?

749
00:50:36.000 --> 00:50:38.000
Please, forgive me,

750
00:50:38.000 --> 00:50:40.000
I'm just very nervous.

751
00:50:40.000 --> 00:50:42.000
You see,

752
00:50:42.000 --> 00:50:48.000
I haven't had a date
since my wife died.

753
00:50:49.000 --> 00:50:51.000
How old was your daughter?

754
00:50:51.000 --> 00:50:53.000
She was just an infant.

755
00:50:53.000 --> 00:50:55.000
It was hard
being a single dad,

756
00:50:55.000 --> 00:50:59.000
but I did my best.

757
00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:03.000
I never knew
my mother, either.

758
00:51:03.000 --> 00:51:04.000
Or my father.

759
00:51:04.000 --> 00:51:07.000
Oh, I'm so sorry.

760
00:51:07.000 --> 00:51:08.000
Who raised you?

761
00:51:08.000 --> 00:51:10.000
My great-grandfather.

762
00:51:10.000 --> 00:51:13.000
I basically grew up
on this ship.

763
00:51:13.000 --> 00:51:15.000
That's why
you're a captain.

764
00:51:15.000 --> 00:51:18.000
Yeah. It's all
I've ever known.

765
00:51:18.000 --> 00:51:22.000
It was just expected.

766
00:51:22.000 --> 00:51:23.000
You know, a family thing.

767
00:51:23.000 --> 00:51:27.000
I understand,
family is everything.

768
00:51:27.000 --> 00:51:30.000
You have to honor the past.

769
00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:33.000
But we make our own future.

770
00:51:46.000 --> 00:51:48.000
- Dad?
- Mavis!

771
00:51:48.000 --> 00:51:51.000
- Mmm.
- Johnny!

772
00:51:52.000 --> 00:51:58.000
Captain Ericka and I were just
discussing the hospitality industry.

773
00:51:58.000 --> 00:52:00.000
You know,
just work stuff.

774
00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:01.000
You're working now?

775
00:52:01.000 --> 00:52:03.000
This is supposed to be
a vacation.

776
00:52:03.000 --> 00:52:04.000
A family vacation.

777
00:52:04.000 --> 00:52:08.000
I should really go
do captain-y things.

778
00:52:08.000 --> 00:52:11.000
Dad, you said you were
gonna spend time with Dennis.

779
00:52:11.000 --> 00:52:14.000
Dennis. Dennis? Dennis.

780
00:52:14.000 --> 00:52:17.000
Oh! Yeah, you're right.
Where is that kid?

781
00:52:17.000 --> 00:52:20.000
Denisovich? You're
supposed to be with me.

782
00:52:20.000 --> 00:52:22.000
Come on now, kid,
it's family time.

783
00:52:22.000 --> 00:52:24.000
Quit hiding. Dennis?

784
00:52:25.000 --> 00:52:26.000
What was that about?

785
00:52:26.000 --> 00:52:27.000
You mean
your dad's date?

786
00:52:27.000 --> 00:52:30.000
It wasn't a date.
It was work stuff.

787
00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:32.000
Uh-huh.

788
00:52:32.000 --> 00:52:33.000
I'm telling you, Johnny,

789
00:52:33.000 --> 00:52:35.000
there is something about
that woman I don't trust.

790
00:52:35.000 --> 00:52:38.000
But you want your dad
to be happy, right?

791
00:52:38.000 --> 00:52:40.000
Yes.

792
00:52:40.000 --> 00:52:42.000
Just not with her.

793
00:52:42.000 --> 00:52:44.000
Mmm.
Whoo-hoo-hoo!

794
00:52:44.000 --> 00:52:45.000
Heads up, honey.

795
00:52:45.000 --> 00:52:47.000
This guac is loaded
with garlic.

796
00:52:47.000 --> 00:52:49.000
Garlic?

797
00:52:55.000 --> 00:52:58.000
Aw! That was
a cute toot, honey.

798
00:53:15.000 --> 00:53:17.000
- We've been up all night!
- Let's stay up all day, too!

799
00:53:17.000 --> 00:53:20.000
Let's get wild!

800
00:53:32.000 --> 00:53:34.000
- Ericka!
- What?

801
00:53:34.000 --> 00:53:37.000
Just where have you been, young lady?

802
00:53:37.000 --> 00:53:40.000
Uh, doing work.

803
00:53:40.000 --> 00:53:42.000
Wearing that?

804
00:53:42.000 --> 00:53:44.000
You were with him!
I know it!

805
00:53:44.000 --> 00:53:46.000
Who?

806
00:53:46.000 --> 00:53:49.000
"Who?" You know who!

807
00:53:49.000 --> 00:53:51.000
You've been sneaking around
my back

808
00:53:51.000 --> 00:53:54.000
trying to kill Dracula again,
haven't you?

809
00:53:54.000 --> 00:53:57.000
So what if I have?
I am a grown woman!

810
00:53:57.000 --> 00:53:59.000
I have the right to kill
whoever I want.

811
00:53:59.000 --> 00:54:01.000
It's not just about you.

812
00:54:01.000 --> 00:54:04.000
You could have ruined
the legacy.

813
00:54:04.000 --> 00:54:07.000
What if he discovered
who you were?

814
00:54:07.000 --> 00:54:10.000
I know. I wasn't thinking.
There's just something about him

815
00:54:10.000 --> 00:54:12.000
that just drives me crazy!

816
00:54:12.000 --> 00:54:15.000
I just, I see him,
and I want to...

817
00:54:15.000 --> 00:54:16.000
Punch him?

818
00:54:16.000 --> 00:54:18.000
Uh... I guess.

819
00:54:18.000 --> 00:54:20.000
Just, I can't wait
to get this over with.

820
00:54:20.000 --> 00:54:23.000
Don't worry,
it won't be long now.

821
00:54:23.000 --> 00:54:26.000
Once you recover the
instrument of destruction,

822
00:54:26.000 --> 00:54:28.000
no one can stop us.

823
00:54:28.000 --> 00:54:31.000
Not even Dracula!

824
00:54:31.000 --> 00:54:34.000
- Oh. Excuse me.
- Spies!

825
00:54:38.000 --> 00:54:41.000
Now, quickly,
before someone comes!

826
00:55:02.000 --> 00:55:04.000
Everyone assemble
on the forward deck.

827
00:55:04.000 --> 00:55:08.000
We are arriving
at our final destination.

828
00:55:08.000 --> 00:55:10.000
From the depths of creation,

829
00:55:10.000 --> 00:55:13.000
the mighty city has risen
once again.

830
00:55:13.000 --> 00:55:16.000
Home to the greatest
monster civilization

831
00:55:16.000 --> 00:55:18.000
the world has ever known,

832
00:55:18.000 --> 00:55:23.000
far surpassing Athens and Rome in
art, culture and sophistication.

833
00:55:23.000 --> 00:55:29.000
I give you the legendary
lost city of Atlantis.

834
00:55:53.000 --> 00:55:57.000
It's a giant Kraken!

835
00:56:43.000 --> 00:56:46.000
Welcome to Atlantis!

836
00:56:50.000 --> 00:56:52.000
Oh!

837
00:57:05.000 --> 00:57:07.000
Ooh. I am so excited!

838
00:57:07.000 --> 00:57:10.000
Come to Daddy!

839
00:57:11.000 --> 00:57:14.000
- Oh.
- Twenty-eight black!

840
00:57:14.000 --> 00:57:16.000
Oh!

841
00:57:17.000 --> 00:57:20.000
- Ahhh!
- Oh, no, you don't.

842
00:57:20.000 --> 00:57:23.000
Last time you gambled, you lost
an arm and a leg. Literally!

843
00:57:23.000 --> 00:57:25.000
- Replacement limbs...
- I'll raise you 40.

844
00:57:25.000 --> 00:57:27.000
...aren't just lying around
like they were in the old days.

845
00:57:27.000 --> 00:57:30.000
So, no gambling.

846
00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:31.000
Frank!

847
00:57:31.000 --> 00:57:34.000
Yes, dear! Got it!
No gambling!

848
00:57:39.000 --> 00:57:41.000
- Tinkles, stop.
- Wait.

849
00:57:41.000 --> 00:57:44.000
- Stop it, Tinkles, stop.
- Ah! Wait!

850
00:57:47.000 --> 00:57:49.000
Have you guys seen Mavis?
I have to find her.

851
00:57:49.000 --> 00:57:50.000
Why? What's going on?

852
00:57:50.000 --> 00:57:52.000
I'm going to tell her
about Ericka.

853
00:57:52.000 --> 00:57:55.000
I can't lie to
my own daughter anymore.

854
00:57:55.000 --> 00:57:58.000
She's the most important
person in the world to me.

855
00:57:58.000 --> 00:58:01.000
I have to tell her the truth.

856
00:58:02.000 --> 00:58:05.000
Right after I talk to Ericka.

857
00:58:06.000 --> 00:58:08.000
Hey.

858
00:58:09.000 --> 00:58:11.000
All right, I'm all...

859
00:58:11.000 --> 00:58:13.000
Frank, are you sure
you know what you're doing?

860
00:58:13.000 --> 00:58:17.000
I got this. I'm all in.

861
00:58:19.000 --> 00:58:21.000
Johnny, have you seen
my dad?

862
00:58:21.000 --> 00:58:23.000
- Maybe he's with Bob.
- Why would he be with Bob?

863
00:58:23.000 --> 00:58:25.000
Bob's a great guy.

864
00:58:25.000 --> 00:58:28.000
- Oh, there he is.
- Who? Bob?

865
00:58:45.000 --> 00:58:49.000
There he is!
Hi, Bob!

866
01:00:13.000 --> 01:00:15.000
Oh.

867
01:01:27.000 --> 01:01:29.000
There it is.

868
01:01:46.000 --> 01:01:48.000
You saved my life.

869
01:01:48.000 --> 01:01:50.000
Of course.
Why wouldn't I?

870
01:01:50.000 --> 01:01:53.000
I just can't believe you
would do that for a human.

871
01:01:53.000 --> 01:01:57.000
Humans, monsters,
what's the difference?

872
01:01:57.000 --> 01:02:00.000
Yeah, right. Right.

873
01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:02.000
Wait. What are you doing here?

874
01:02:02.000 --> 01:02:06.000
Oh, uh... Well, you know,
vampires can predict the future,

875
01:02:06.000 --> 01:02:09.000
so I knew you would
need my help.

876
01:02:09.000 --> 01:02:11.000
Ha! Never heard that before.

877
01:02:11.000 --> 01:02:14.000
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
It's a well-known fact.

878
01:02:14.000 --> 01:02:16.000
What are you doing here?

879
01:02:16.000 --> 01:02:17.000
Oh! Uh...

880
01:02:17.000 --> 01:02:19.000
Well, I'm here to get that.

881
01:02:19.000 --> 01:02:21.000
Yeah, it's a family heirloom.

882
01:02:21.000 --> 01:02:26.000
Yeah, it was lost at sea, and
my great-grandfather is... Was!

883
01:02:26.000 --> 01:02:29.000
Uh, was totally obsessed
with getting it back.

884
01:02:29.000 --> 01:02:34.000
So, anywho, thanks for saving my
life, but I can take it from...

885
01:02:39.000 --> 01:02:41.000
Got to be
a little more careful.

886
01:02:41.000 --> 01:02:43.000
How many times
can you save my life, right?

887
01:02:43.000 --> 01:02:45.000
I don't know. Every time?

888
01:02:45.000 --> 01:02:49.000
Really? Well, then...

889
01:03:22.000 --> 01:03:25.000
Wow!

890
01:03:41.000 --> 01:03:45.000
Ah,
that was incredible.

891
01:03:55.000 --> 01:03:57.000
Oh, uh...

892
01:03:57.000 --> 01:04:01.000
Don't you want to get
your family heirloom thingy?

893
01:04:01.000 --> 01:04:04.000
Oh. Right.

894
01:04:08.000 --> 01:04:11.000
Got it.

895
01:04:39.000 --> 01:04:41.000
Mmm.

896
01:04:41.000 --> 01:04:44.000
Oh, here, let me get
that for you.

897
01:04:45.000 --> 01:04:47.000
Dad!

898
01:04:47.000 --> 01:04:49.000
Mavis!

899
01:04:49.000 --> 01:04:51.000
What are you doing
to my father?

900
01:04:51.000 --> 01:04:53.000
Wait! Whoa. Whoa!

901
01:04:53.000 --> 01:04:55.000
Mavis, stop!
Put her down!

902
01:04:55.000 --> 01:05:00.000
No! She's trying to hurt you.
Why can't you see that?

903
01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:03.000
Because I...

904
01:05:03.000 --> 01:05:05.000
Because I Zinged.

905
01:05:05.000 --> 01:05:07.000
What?

906
01:05:07.000 --> 01:05:10.000
I Zinged with Ericka.

907
01:05:10.000 --> 01:05:13.000
No, that can't be true.

908
01:05:13.000 --> 01:05:14.000
You only Zing once.

909
01:05:14.000 --> 01:05:17.000
That's what I thought, too.

910
01:05:17.000 --> 01:05:19.000
"Zing"? What's a Zing?

911
01:05:19.000 --> 01:05:23.000
Uh, well, it's a thing
for monsters.

912
01:05:23.000 --> 01:05:26.000
It's kind of like
our "love at first sight."

913
01:05:26.000 --> 01:05:29.000
What? No. No, no, no.

914
01:05:29.000 --> 01:05:31.000
- You don't even know me.
- Well, not yet.

915
01:05:31.000 --> 01:05:34.000
- But we're just...
- No, you don't understand.

916
01:05:34.000 --> 01:05:35.000
I can't be with you.

917
01:05:35.000 --> 01:05:38.000
I could never be
with someone like you.

918
01:05:38.000 --> 01:05:40.000
I could never be with

919
01:05:40.000 --> 01:05:42.000
a monster.

920
01:05:52.000 --> 01:05:55.000
Dad, I'm so sorry.

921
01:05:55.000 --> 01:05:58.000
- I...
- It doesn't matter.

922
01:05:59.000 --> 01:06:02.000
You heard what she said.

923
01:06:08.000 --> 01:06:11.000
But a Zing never lies.

924
01:06:24.000 --> 01:06:27.000
Ha! You got it!

925
01:06:27.000 --> 01:06:30.000
Yes.

926
01:06:33.000 --> 01:06:36.000
Now that we have
the instrument of destruction,

927
01:06:36.000 --> 01:06:39.000
our family legacy
will be fulfilled.

928
01:06:39.000 --> 01:06:43.000
But first, we'll draw them in
with a dance party!

929
01:06:43.000 --> 01:06:47.000
I love to dance.

930
01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:01.000
Frank,
could you zip me up?

931
01:07:01.000 --> 01:07:03.000
We're gonna be late.

932
01:07:03.000 --> 01:07:06.000
Where did you get those?

933
01:07:06.000 --> 01:07:08.000
Uh, see,
here's the funny thing.

934
01:07:08.000 --> 01:07:11.000
I lost my hands gambling,
but... It's no big deal!

935
01:07:11.000 --> 01:07:13.000
Look, I got these
from the seafood buffet.

936
01:07:13.000 --> 01:07:15.000
Look at this. Clickety-click,
click, clack, clack, click, click.

937
01:07:15.000 --> 01:07:19.000
I kind of like 'em.
I like 'em.

938
01:07:24.000 --> 01:07:25.000
Mmm! Mmm! Mmm.

939
01:07:25.000 --> 01:07:27.000
Mmm. Mmm.

940
01:07:27.000 --> 01:07:29.000
A-ha!

941
01:07:52.000 --> 01:07:53.000
Ah, I guess the party's
this way.

942
01:07:53.000 --> 01:07:55.000
Whoo!

943
01:07:55.000 --> 01:07:58.000
Whoa!

944
01:08:06.000 --> 01:08:08.000
Wow.

945
01:08:10.000 --> 01:08:13.000
Let's get this party
started right!

946
01:08:13.000 --> 01:08:14.000
- Whoo-hoo!
- All right!

947
01:08:14.000 --> 01:08:16.000
What?

948
01:08:16.000 --> 01:08:18.000
Huh?

949
01:08:18.000 --> 01:08:22.000
I thought they said
the party was this way.

950
01:08:47.000 --> 01:08:49.000
DJ in a clamshell?

951
01:08:49.000 --> 01:08:53.000
I'm so jealous.

952
01:09:39.000 --> 01:09:43.000
I can't believe my dad Zinged with
someone who's trying to kill him.

953
01:09:43.000 --> 01:09:45.000
Yeah, the Zing
makes you do crazy things.

954
01:09:45.000 --> 01:09:47.000
Really, Johnny?

955
01:09:47.000 --> 01:09:52.000
What's most important to understand
is that love is an infinite enigma

956
01:09:52.000 --> 01:09:54.000
that is beyond
our understanding.

957
01:09:54.000 --> 01:09:58.000
You and I were two halves,
a world apart.

958
01:09:58.000 --> 01:10:01.000
But then we followed
the strands of destiny

959
01:10:01.000 --> 01:10:02.000
and were brought together.

960
01:10:02.000 --> 01:10:05.000
And our halves made one whole.

961
01:10:05.000 --> 01:10:08.000
But what if she and he...

962
01:10:08.000 --> 01:10:11.000
You must release all the
negativity and look within.

963
01:10:11.000 --> 01:10:14.000
Your bond is unbreakable.

964
01:10:15.000 --> 01:10:17.000
You're right, honey. Wow.

965
01:10:17.000 --> 01:10:19.000
Thanks.

966
01:10:19.000 --> 01:10:21.000
Whoa, you sounded
pretty smart, Dad.

967
01:10:21.000 --> 01:10:23.000
Oh, that? Yeah, it was
just the philosophy

968
01:10:23.000 --> 01:10:26.000
of Sifu Sing from my favorite
TV show when I was a kid,

969
01:10:26.000 --> 01:10:28.000
Kung Fu Shaolin Monk Master.

970
01:10:28.000 --> 01:10:29.000
Anyways, let's get back
to dancing!

971
01:10:29.000 --> 01:10:32.000
Cool.

972
01:10:35.000 --> 01:10:37.000
Dad? You have to talk
to Ericka.

973
01:10:37.000 --> 01:10:38.000
- What?
- I know.

974
01:10:38.000 --> 01:10:40.000
I know what I said before,

975
01:10:40.000 --> 01:10:43.000
but maybe I overreacted
a teensy bit.

976
01:10:43.000 --> 01:10:45.000
It's just the thought
of losing you.

977
01:10:45.000 --> 01:10:49.000
What? What are you talking
about, losing me?

978
01:10:49.000 --> 01:10:51.000
Well, obviously,
after you get married,

979
01:10:51.000 --> 01:10:53.000
you're gonna live on the ship
and travel around the world...

980
01:10:53.000 --> 01:10:55.000
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Slow down, Mavis.

981
01:10:55.000 --> 01:10:57.000
There are two things
I can promise you.

982
01:10:57.000 --> 01:11:03.000
One, nothing can ever take me
from you and all my family.

983
01:11:03.000 --> 01:11:07.000
Two, I will never live
on a boat.

984
01:11:09.000 --> 01:11:11.000
You're my cute
little tarantula.

985
01:11:11.000 --> 01:11:14.000
How could I ever leave you?

986
01:11:14.000 --> 01:11:16.000
Now, seriously,
go talk to her.

987
01:11:16.000 --> 01:11:18.000
I can't. You heard
what she said,

988
01:11:18.000 --> 01:11:21.000
she could never be
with someone like me.

989
01:11:21.000 --> 01:11:23.000
No, Dad.
You're just a half,

990
01:11:23.000 --> 01:11:27.000
and you have to follow your destiny
to find an infinite whole.

991
01:11:27.000 --> 01:11:28.000
You sound like Johnny.

992
01:11:28.000 --> 01:11:31.000
Point is,
you can't deny a Zing.

993
01:11:31.000 --> 01:11:34.000
Monster, human, unicorn...

994
01:11:34.000 --> 01:11:36.000
It doesn't matter.

995
01:11:36.000 --> 01:11:39.000
So go to her! Now!

996
01:11:40.000 --> 01:11:42.000
Okay. I'm on it.

997
01:11:43.000 --> 01:11:44.000
Hey, man, you're
not allowed up here.

998
01:11:44.000 --> 01:11:48.000
The DJ booth is a sacred space.

999
01:11:54.000 --> 01:11:56.000
No. Tinkles, quiet.

1000
01:11:56.000 --> 01:11:57.000
Who is this?

1001
01:11:57.000 --> 01:12:02.000
Ha! I know you recognize me,
your greatest rival.

1002
01:12:02.000 --> 01:12:05.000
Hmm. Oh, right.

1003
01:12:05.000 --> 01:12:08.000
You own that Holiday Inn
down by the airport.

1004
01:12:08.000 --> 01:12:12.000
No! It is I,
Abraham Van Helsing.

1005
01:12:12.000 --> 01:12:14.000
Van Helsing?

1006
01:12:14.000 --> 01:12:16.000
After all these years?

1007
01:12:16.000 --> 01:12:19.000
You look awful.

1008
01:12:19.000 --> 01:12:22.000
Always with the quick insults.

1009
01:12:22.000 --> 01:12:24.000
Well, this will shut you up.

1010
01:12:24.000 --> 01:12:26.000
And all monsters.

1011
01:12:26.000 --> 01:12:30.000
Eh, huh? That's just Ericka's
family heirloom thingy.

1012
01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:33.000
Good one, Ericka.

1013
01:12:33.000 --> 01:12:34.000
Ericka?

1014
01:12:34.000 --> 01:12:36.000
You fool.

1015
01:12:36.000 --> 01:12:39.000
Not only is she
the ship's captain,

1016
01:12:39.000 --> 01:12:41.000
but she also happens
to be...

1017
01:12:43.000 --> 01:12:46.000
Wait. You tell him.

1018
01:12:47.000 --> 01:12:50.000
I'm his great-granddaughter.

1019
01:12:51.000 --> 01:12:54.000
I'm Ericka Van Helsing.

1020
01:12:54.000 --> 01:12:57.000
I knew there was
something wrong with her.

1021
01:12:57.000 --> 01:12:58.000
But...

1022
01:12:58.000 --> 01:13:01.000
See, what happened...

1023
01:13:01.000 --> 01:13:03.000
Now that we're all caught up,

1024
01:13:03.000 --> 01:13:05.000
let's get back to the dying.

1025
01:13:05.000 --> 01:13:12.000
Behold, the key to the demise
of all monsters.

1026
01:13:23.000 --> 01:13:25.000
Let's see.

1027
01:13:25.000 --> 01:13:28.000
Right... Okay.

1028
01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:33.000
Listen to the melody

1029
01:13:33.000 --> 01:13:35.000
of your destruction.

1030
01:13:38.000 --> 01:13:41.000
Ooh, what's this little
doodad do?

1031
01:13:41.000 --> 01:13:44.000
Yeah!

1032
01:14:05.000 --> 01:14:09.000
Hey, look! It's the Kraken.

1033
01:14:22.000 --> 01:14:25.000
Everybody out! Now!

1034
01:14:36.000 --> 01:14:39.000
We're trapped! Everybody back!

1035
01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:03.000
Yay!

1036
01:15:09.000 --> 01:15:11.000
Baby!

1037
01:15:11.000 --> 01:15:13.000
Papa!

1038
01:15:22.000 --> 01:15:25.000
This has to stop now!

1039
01:15:25.000 --> 01:15:26.000
Drac, no!

1040
01:15:26.000 --> 01:15:28.000
Ah!

1041
01:15:40.000 --> 01:15:43.000
Dad!

1042
01:15:43.000 --> 01:15:44.000
Mavis!

1043
01:15:44.000 --> 01:15:48.000
Time for the immortal Dracula
to die.

1044
01:15:58.000 --> 01:16:01.000
Dad!

1045
01:16:06.000 --> 01:16:08.000
No!

1046
01:16:08.000 --> 01:16:10.000
Ericka!

1047
01:16:14.000 --> 01:16:15.000
Bob! Help!

1048
01:16:15.000 --> 01:16:17.000
Huh?

1049
01:16:19.000 --> 01:16:21.000
Tinkles?

1050
01:16:21.000 --> 01:16:22.000
Dennis.

1051
01:16:22.000 --> 01:16:24.000
Oh, no.
Bob is Tinkles?

1052
01:16:24.000 --> 01:16:26.000
How did he get here?

1053
01:16:26.000 --> 01:16:29.000
But thank goodness he did,
'cause look!

1054
01:17:09.000 --> 01:17:10.000
You can't do this!

1055
01:17:10.000 --> 01:17:13.000
You're wrong
about monsters!

1056
01:17:13.000 --> 01:17:16.000
Dracula... He saved my life.

1057
01:17:16.000 --> 01:17:17.000
What?

1058
01:17:17.000 --> 01:17:19.000
